    "l": "0.3",
    "I": "0.006",
    "g": "9.8"
  },
  "description": "Nonlinear cart-pendulum open-loop impulse response (CTMS).",
  "provenance": "CTMS, Inverted Pendulum: Simulink Modeling, https://ctms.engin.umich.edu/CTMS/?example=InvertedPendulum&section=SimulinkModeling . Parameters M=0.5, m=0.2, b=0.1, l=0.3, I=0.006; theta from the downward vertical with theta(0)=pi; impulse approximated by a Pulse Generator (amplitude 1000, period 10, width 0.01%). The four Fcn blocks of the source form an algebraic loop; here the same Newton-Euler equations are solved explicitly for x'' and theta''.",
  "root": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": 36,
        "type": "Pulse Generator",
        "name": "Impulse (1 N s)",
        "x": 40,
        "y": 160,
        "params": {
          "amplitude": "1000",
          "period": "10",
          "pulse_width": "0.01",
          "phase_delay": "0"
        },
        "flipped": false
      },
      {
        "id": 47,
        "type": "Subsystem",
        "name": "Pendulum",
        "x": 220,
        "y": 153,
        "params": {},
        "flipped": false,
        "sub_scene": {
          "blocks": [
